Add a redirection (the first that applies wins)

Usage:
  nexoctl dist redirect add ALIAS ID (--from RE --to TARGET | --host-from HOST --to-host HOST | --https-only) [--status N] [flags]

Examples:
  nexoctl dist redirect add local website --from '^/old/(.*)$' --to '/new/$1'
  nexoctl dist redirect add local website --host-from example.com --to-host www.example.com
  nexoctl dist redirect add local website --https-only

Flags:
      --from string        RE2 expression of the paths
  -h, --help               help for add
      --host-from string   host to redirect
      --https-only         redirect plain HTTP to HTTPS
      --status int         301 (default), 302, 303, 307 or 308
      --to string          target, with $1 and ${name} from the groups of --from
      --to-host string     target host (path and query kept)

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)
